  "body": "Side branch: side/path-kernel\n\nThis is a sync PR by the rule **Side branch** of `AGENTS.md`. It merges `main` into `side/path-kernel` with `git merge`. There is no rebase and no force-push. The base was `side/path-kernel` at `21fd9e57d`.\n\n## Merges\n\n1. `0af768ad8`: merge of `main` at `39298012074799bf84677c63dc3d34200af8326c`.\n2. `a500601ef`: merge of `side/path-kernel` at `500f40256f3fe6e5315084855451eaabebfe1875`. This brings the #4407 fix (PR #4437) and PR #4412. It has no conflict.\n3. `d2dfb9dda`: merge of `main` at `6898b02ea3195e9124e6113afd6ab3cee38d0c50`.\n\nHead: `d2dfb9ddab375ff0c0896dd80944659fe9b729d4`. After the gates, `main` moved to `2394b5ad1`. This PR does not include that move.\n\n## Conflicts and resolution\n\nEach conflict is a list where each side added a crate or a step. In each file, both sides are kept.\n\n- `Cargo.toml` (merge 1): the workspace members hold `crates/pathkernel` (side) and `crates/ui-kit` (main, #4394).\n- `xtask/src/plan.rs` (merge 1): `BATCH_CRATES`, `ALL_CRATES` and `CLIPPY` hold `pathkernel` and `ui-kit`.\n- `xtask/src/heavy_plan_tests.rs` (merge 1): the side's `pathkernel` reach pins are kept. Main's rule that the kernel reaches each crate but `gpu` and `ui-kit` is kept.\n- `xtask/src/step_tests.rs` (merge 1): the pinned crate list holds `pathkernel` and `ui-kit`.\n- `xtask/src/tests.rs` (merge 3): the clippy step names `camcraft-pathkernel` (side). It is now the second last batch step, because main (#4440) adds the `site tests` step as the last one.\n\nNo logic was changed on the two sides.\n\n## Compile fixes\n\nNone. After merge 1 and after merge 3, `cargo check --tests` passed for each package one at a time: geometry, pathkernel, motion, sim, post, app, ui, ui-kit and xtask. `cargo test -j 6 -p xtask` is green.\n\n## Re-recorded baselines and readings\n\nNone. Main's planner-side PRs since the last sync (#4416 model chamfer arcs, #4273 and #4270 laser, #4360 radial drop, and others) change no pin of the old planners. On the final tree these are green with no edit:\n\n- `camcraft-motion` `pass_start_levels`: 45 passed. This includes the #4153 `kernel_baseline` goldens (with chamfer), `kernel_rings`, `kernel_guides` and `shared_planner`.\n- `camcraft-motion` `kernel_laws`: 32 passed.\n- `camcraft-pathkernel` `laws`: 177 passed. The kernel readings that #4437 changed came in with the side merge, and this PR does not touch them.\n- `camcraft-app`, release `--ignored`: `offset_pass_start` (`shared_planner`, `kernel_laws_fig8`, `planner_switch`) 9 passed, and `pocket_pass_start` (`kernel_baseline`) 2 passed.\n\n## Class\n\nDELTA. The hand edits are only the conflict hunks above, in `Cargo.toml` and the four `xtask` files. Merge 2 has an empty remerge-diff.\n\n## Gates (final head `d2dfb9dda`)\n\n- `CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=6 xvfb-run -a cargo xtask gate batch`: `wall 85.1 min, 1019 step(s), 0 failed, 0 stalled`.\n  - `clippy -D warnings`: ok.\n  - `app suites: example_catalog`: 50 passed, 4 ignored.\n  - `app suites: example_catalog_adaptive`: 1 passed.\n  - `app suites: example_catalog_edge_work`: 1 passed.\n  - `site tests (python unittest, zola, node)`: SKIP (tool missing: zola, node). This is not a pass.\n- Heavy, motion and app lanes (`cargo xtask gate heavy --base origin/main --only \"heavy build\" --only \"motion heavy\" --only \"app heavy\"`; the kernel lane did not run): `wall 53.9 min, 117 step(s), 0 failed, 0 stalled`. The four known-fail markers are red as expected:\n  - motion #1950 `machining2d::pocket_hsm::ring_tests::the_stock_ring_level_reaches_the_air_planner_with_the_stock`;\n  - motion #1950 `machining2d::pocket_hsm::ring_tests::the_stock_ring_level_plans_adaptive_with_no_budget_note`;\n  - app #1950 `the_users_whole_model_bore_roughs_adaptive_on_each_level` (`pocket3d_hsm`);\n  - app #2849 `fig8_outside_containment_with_em0800_and_clearing_kinds_works` (`shoulder_adaptive`).\n- `cargo xtask gate light`: `wall 5.5 min, 7 step(s), 0 failed, 0 stalled`.\n- `cargo test -j 6 -p xtask`: green.\n\nChangelog: none\n\nRefs #4023\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
